 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Beta-1,4-GalTase 6</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.4.1.-</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UDP-Gal:glucosylceramide beta-1,4-galactosyltransferase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UDP-galactose:beta-N-acetylglucosamine beta-1,4-galactosyltransferase 6</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Beta4Gal-T6</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Glucosylceramide beta-1,4-galactosyltransferase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">B4GALT6</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_9331</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">B4GT6_HUMAN Reviewed; 382 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference96086</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/NP_004766</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes the synthesis of lactosylceramide (LacCer) viathe transfer of galactose from UDP-galactose to glucosylceramide(GlcCer) (PubMed:3099851, PubMed:1551920, PubMed:24498430). LacCeris the starting point in the biosynthesis of all gangliosides(membrane-bound glycosphingolipids) which play pivotal roles inthe CNS including neuronal maturation and axonal and myelinformation (By similarity). {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:Q9WVK5,ECO:0000269|PubMed:1551920, ECO:0000269|PubMed:24498430,ECO:0000269|PubMed:3099851}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=a beta-D-glucosyl-(1&lt;-&gt;1&apos;)-N-acylsphing-4-enine + UDP-alpha-D-galactose = beta-D-galactosyl-(1-&gt;4)-beta-D-glucosyl-(1&lt;-&gt;1)-ceramide(d18:1(4E)) + H(+) + UDP; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:31495,ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:17950, ChEBI:CHEBI:22801,ChEBI:CHEBI:58223, ChEBI:CHEBI:66914; EC=2.4.1.274;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:1551920,ECO:0000269|PubMed:24498430, ECO:0000269|PubMed:3099851};COFACTOR:Name=Mn(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:29035;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:3099851};Name=Mg(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:18420;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:3099851};ACTIVITY REGULATION: Inhibited by EDTA.{ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:O88419}.BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=3 uM for glucosylceramide {ECO:0000269|PubMed:3099851};KM=0.5 uM for UDP-galactose {ECO:0000269|PubMed:3099851};Vmax=0.06 nmol/h/mg enzyme toward glucosylceramide{ECO:0000269|PubMed:3099851};Vmax=86 nmol/h/mg enzyme toward UDP-galactose{ECO:0000269|PubMed:3099851};PATHWAY: Protein modification; protein glycosylation.PATHWAY: Sphingolipid metabolism.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Golgi apparatus, Golgi stack membrane{ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P15291}; Single-pass type II membraneprotein. Note=Trans cisternae of Golgi stack.{ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P15291}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=1;IsoId=Q9UBX8-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=Q9UBX8-2; Sequence=VSP_056554;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: High expression in brain and adrenal gland,lower in liver, lung, colon and peripheral white blood cells.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the glycosyltransferase 7 family.{ECO:0000305}.WEB RESOURCE: Name=Functional Glycomics Gateway - GTase;Note=Beta-1,4-galactosyltransferase 6;URL=&quot;http://www.functionalglycomics.org/glycomics/molecule/jsp/glycoEnzyme/viewGlycoEnzyme.jsp?gbpId=gt_hum_441&quot;; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

